  "title": "A COVID-19 survivors and close contacts EEG dataset",
  "description": "This dataset comprises 169 resting-state electroencephalograms (EEGs) from COVID-19 survivors (n=86) and healthy close contacts (n=83), acquired using standard 10-20 electrode montage. The study characterizes EEG signatures associated with COVID-19 infection and recovery, comparing neurophysiological patterns between affected and control groups. Data collection included 8 minutes of eyes-closed resting EEG followed by alternating eye-state conditions, providing a comprehensive neurophysiological profile relevant to understanding post-COVID neurological sequelae.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was acquired using a 10-20 standard montage. Resting EEG was recorded for 8 minutes with eyes closed in all participants. Additional recordings included 2 minutes of alternating closed and open eyes, followed by 2 minutes of recovery.",
